hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"991","991 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: We are Rifa’ah bin Yahya bin Abdullah bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of his father’s uncle Muadh bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of his father, said: “I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I sneezed and said: Praise be to God, thanks a lot.” Good and blessed in him, blessed be he, as our Lord loves and is pleased with. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, he left and said: “Who is speaking?” In prayer? But no one spoke to him, then he said the second time: “Who is speaking during the prayer?” “Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ bin Afra said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: How did you say? He said: I said, “Praise be to God, many, good, and blessed thanks be to Him, and blessed be He, as our Lord loves and is pleased with.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, thirty-odd angels raced to see which of them would ascend with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"992","992 Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: We are Mukhlid, he said: We are Yunus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa’il, on the authority of his father. He said: “I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he said the takbir, he raised his hands below his ears, so when he recited neither The lost people said: “Amen,” so I heard him while I was behind him. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man say: Praise be to God, much praise. Good and blessed in it. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, he said: “Who is the one who speaks in prayer? Then the man said: O Messenger of God, I do not want harm with it. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Twelve kings have attacked it. Nothing has deprived it of anything other than the Throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"993","993 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Al-Harith asked Ibn Hisham, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how does the revelation come to you? He said: “In the likeness of the ringing of a bell, then he will be separated from me, and I have understood what he said: He is the hardest on me, and sometimes he will come to me in a similar situation.” The image of the young man, and he will cast him away to me.”"
"994","994 Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin told us, by reading it, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, On the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: How does he come to you? Revelation? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and it is the hardest on me, so it stops me and I have become aware of it.” What he said, and sometimes the king appears to me as a man, and speaks to me, and I understand what he says.” Aisha said: And I saw him descend upon him that day. It is very cold, so he is separated from it, and his forehead is dripping with sweat. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"995","995 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas In his saying: “Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it.” He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was suffering from a severe revelation. He used to move his lips. God said: Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. {16} Indeed, it is upon Us to gather it and recite it. {17} He said: Gather it in your chest, then recite it. So when We recited it, he followed his recitation, saying: So listen to him and be silent. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would listen when Gabriel came to him. Then, when he sets out, he recites it as he recited it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"996","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr informed us, he said: I am Abd al-Ala, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of al-Miswar ibn Mukhramah, that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “I heard Hisham bin Hakim bin Hazzam reciting Surat Al-Furqan, and he recited letters in it that were not The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me. I said: Who taught you this Surah? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: You lied. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not tell you that. So I took him by the hand and led him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: O Messenger of God, you taught me Surah Al-Furqan, and I heard this man reciting letters in it that you had not taught me. So he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read, Hisham.” So he read as he had read, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Thus.” was revealed.\" Then he said: \"Read, O Omar.\" So I read, and he said: \"This is how it was revealed.\" Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, the Qur’an It was revealed in seven letters. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"997","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, by reading it, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, who said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying: “I heard Hisham bin Hakim recites Surat Al-Furqan in a different way than I recited it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me. So I was about to rush him, then I gave him time until he left, then I wrapped him in his cloak and brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, I heard this man reciting Surat Al-Furqan in a different way than you had read it to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Read.” He recited the recitation that I heard him reciting, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is how it was revealed,” then he said to me: “Read.” So I recited, and he said: “This is how it was revealed. Indeed, this Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, so recite as much of it as you can.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"998","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa bin told me Al-Zubair, that Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari informed him that they heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: “I heard Hisham bin Hakim bin Hazzam recited Surat Al-Furqan, during the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I listened to his reading, and lo and behold He recites it in many letters, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not recite it to me, so I almost followed him in prayer, so I was patient until he said hello. When he handed him his robe, I said: Who recited to you this surah that I heard you reciting? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me? May God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: You lied. By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to me this surah that I heard you. You recite it, so I set off with him and led him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, I heard this man reciting a surah. Al-Furqan is based on letters that you did not recite, but you taught me Surat Al-Furqan. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Send it, O Omar. “Read, O Hisham.” So he recited to him the recitation that I heard him reciting. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is how it was revealed.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read, O Omar.” So I recited the recitation that he had recited to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ This is how it was revealed.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, this Qur’an was revealed in seven harfs, so recite as much as is possible.” \"from him\""
"999","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Kaab, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was at the watering place of Banu Ghifar, and Gabriel came to him and said: God commands you to make your nation read The Qur’an is on one letter. He said: I ask God for his pardon and forgiveness, and indeed my nation cannot tolerate that. Then he came to him the second time and said: God commands you to Your nation recites the Qur’an in two harfs. He said: I ask God for his pardon and forgiveness, and my nation cannot tolerate that. The third time came to him, and he said: The God commands you to recite the Qur’an to your nation in three harfs. So he said: I ask God for his pardon and forgiveness, for my nation cannot tolerate that. Then He came to him the fourth time and said: God commands you to recite the Qur’an to your nation in seven letters, so whichever letter they recite to, they have been correct. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Mansour disagreed with the ruling in this hadith. He narrated it on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, with a mursal message. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1000","1000 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Ja`far bin Nufayl told us, he said: I read on Maqil, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited a surah to me, and while I was in I was sitting in the mosque when I heard a man reciting it in contradiction to my recitation, so I said to him: Who taught you this surah? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace So I said: Do not leave me until we bring the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we came to him and I said: O Messenger of God, this has violated My recitation of the surah that you taught me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read, my father.” So I recited it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Well done.” Then he said to the man: “Read.” He disagreed with my reading, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Well done.” Then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O my father, it was revealed in seven letters, all of which are sufficient and sufficient.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Maqil bin Ubaidullah, he is not that strong"
"1001","1001 Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubayy, he said: “What has been hovering in my heart since I converted to Islam?” However, I read a verse and someone else read it other than me, so I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to me. Then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted me, so I said: O Messenger of God, did you recite to me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes, and the other said: Did you not teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes, Gabriel and Michael came to me, so Gabriel sat on my right and Michael on my left, so Gabriel said: Read the Qur’an at One letter, and Mikael said: Rather, increase it, until it reached seven letters, for every letter is clear and sufficient.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1002","1002 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For example The owner of the Qur’an is like the owner of hung camels. If he treats them, he keeps them, and if he lets them go, they go.”"
"1003","1003 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abd. God, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How evil is for one of them to say: I forgot one verse and another, but rather he forgot. Remember the Qur’an. For he is quicker to separate blessings from the breasts of men than from his mind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1004","1004 Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Sa`id bin Yasar told me, that Ibn Abbas He told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the two rak’ahs of Fajr, the first of which was the verse that is in Al-Baqarah. Say, “We believe.” “By God and what has been revealed to us until the end of the verse, and in the last: ‘We believe in God and bear witness that we are submissive.’”"
"1005","1005 Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym told us, he said: Marwan told us, Yazid bin Kaysan said, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “recited in the two rak’ahs of dawn, ‘Say, O you disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, One’.”"
"1006","1006 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If I were to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying the two rak’ahs of Fajr, and he would shorten them until I could say: What he recited in them “By the Mother of the Book” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1007","1007 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Shabib Abi Ruh, on the authority of A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “he prayed the morning prayer and the Romans recited it, and he became confused, so when He prayed and said: “What is the matter with people who pray with us who are not good at purifying themselves? For they are only distorting the Qur’an for us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1008","1008 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid, he said: I am Suleiman, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Minhal, who is Ibn Salamah, On the authority of Abu Barzah, who is Nadhla bin Ubaid Al-Aslami, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “recite in the morning prayer the sixtieth to \"the hundred\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1009","1009 Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Abi Ar-Rijal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Umm Hisham bint Haritha Bin Al-Numan, she said: “I never took this Qur’an and the Glorious Qur’an except from behind the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He used to perform the morning prayer with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1010","1010 Ismail bin Masoud and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ziyad. Ibn Ulaqah said: I heard my uncle saying: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning, and he recited one of the two rak’ahs and the palm trees.” \"Shu'bah said: I met him in the market in a crowded place, and he said: (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1011","1011 Muhammad bin Aban told us, he said: Waki’, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Sari’, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “reciting at dawn when the sun has set.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1012","1012 Musa bin Hazzam al-Tirmidhi and Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Abu Usama told us. He said: Tell me. Sufyan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that he asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the two exorcists, Uqba said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed in them in the dawn prayer.”"
"1013","1013 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Imran Aslam, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir He said: I followed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was riding, so I placed my hands on his feet and said: Recite to me Surah Hud, or Surah Joseph, and he said: “You will not read anything more eloquent with God than the saying: I seek refuge in the Lord of creation.”"
"1014","1014 Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Ayat were revealed to me tonight, the like of which had never been seen before. Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1015","1015 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, and Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, He said: Our Sufyan, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday the verse “The Revelation,” and did he come? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1016","1016 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, and Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am a partner, and the wording for it, on the authority of Al-Makhul bin Rashid, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, Kufi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “ It is recited in the morning prayer on Friday when the prostration is revealed, and has it come upon a person? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1017","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in: p., and said: “David prostrated it in repentance, and we prostrate it in gratitude.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1018","Abdul Malik bin Abdul Hamid told me, he said: Ibn Hanbal told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Khalid told me, he said: Rabah told us, on the authority of Muammar, On the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, on the authority of Ja’far ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada’ah, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited May God bless him and grant him peace in Mecca, Surat An-Najm, so he prostrated and those of him prostrated, so I raised my head and refused to prostrate, and it was not that day. The petitioner submitted to Islam.”"
"1019","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “read the star and prostrated by it.”"
"1020","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Khusaifa, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar told him that he asked Zayd bin Thabit about recitation with the imam, and he said: “There is no recitation with the imam about anything,” and he claimed “It was recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the star descended, he did not prostrate.”"
"1021","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah: He recited to them, “When the sky split open, so he prostrated in it.” When he left, he told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prostrated in it."
"1022","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ayyash, on the authority of Ibn Qays. On the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in \"When the sky split open\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1023","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Omar Bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “We prostrated with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, “When the sky splits open, and recite in the name of your Lord.” Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id. On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Kitten, like him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1024","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Qurrah told us, and he is Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “ Abu Bakr and Omar prostrated when the sky split open, and who is better than them, may God bless him and grant him peace? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1025","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of Qurra, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Abu Bakr prostrated And Omar, and who is better than them, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sky splits open, and recite in the name of your Lord."
"1026","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’ bin Mina, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Mina, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “I prostrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when The sky has split open, and recite in the name of your Lord.”"
"1027","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri informed us, on the authority of Sulaym, who is Ibn Akhdar, on the authority of al-Taymi, who said: Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to me. Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, said: I prayed the evening prayer behind Abu Hurairah, meaning the dark prayer, so he recited When the Sky Split, so he prostrated in it. When he finished, I said: O Abu Hurairah, this is the prostration that we used to perform. He said: “Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated it and I.” Behind him, I continued to prostrate with it until I met Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1028","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Raqaba, on the authority of Ata, Abu Hurairah said: “Every prayer is recited in it, so what “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard us, we heard you, and whatever he hid from us, we hid from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1029","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “In every prayer there is a recitation So whatever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard us, we made you hear, and whatever was hidden from us, we concealed from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1030","Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sallam bin Qutaybah, he said: Hashim bin Al-Barid told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We were. We pray behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the noon prayer, and we hear from him the verse after the verses from Surat Luqman, and Al-Dhariyat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1031","Muhammad bin Shuja’ told us, he said: Abu Ubaidah al-Haddad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid, he said: I heard Abu Bakr bin al-Nadr, he said We were with Anas, and he prayed the noon prayer with them. When he finished, he said: “I prayed the noon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he recited the noon prayer. We have these two surahs in the two rak'ahs: Glory be to the name of your Lord, the Most High. Has the hadith of the transgression reached you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1032","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Atiya bin Qais, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: “ The noon prayer used to be held, and the person who was going would go to Al-Baqi’, relieve himself, then perform ablution, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come. “May God’s peace and blessings be upon him in the first rak’ah, lengthening it.”"
"1033","Yahya bin Durst Al-Basri told us, he said: We are Abu Ismail, and Abu Ismail Ibrahim bin Abdul-Malik Basri, he said: Khalid, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us that Abdullah bin Abi Qatada narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It was He would lead us in the noon prayer, and he would recite in the first two rak’ahs, making us hear the verse as well. He would lengthen the rak’ah in the noon prayer, and the first rak’ah, That means in the morning prayer (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1034","Imran bin Yazid bin Khalid bin Muslim Al-Dimashqi informed us, he said: Our name is Ismail bin Abdullah bin Sama’ah, he said: His name is Abdul Al-Rahman bin Amr bin Abi Amr, narrated by Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Abi Katheer Yamiami, and whose nickname is Abu Nadr, said: Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told me, he said: My father told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to recite the Mother of the Qur’an. And two surahs in the first two rak’ahs of the noon prayer and the afternoon prayer, and he would sometimes make us hear the verse, and he used to prolong the first rak’ah.”"
"1035","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Ibn Abu Qatada said that his father told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite for us in the first two rak’ahs of the prayer.” Dhuhr, so he would make us hear the verse sometimes, and he would lengthen the first time, and shorten the second time, and he would do that in the morning prayer, making the first time long, He shortened the second, and he used to recite for us in the first two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer.”"
"1036","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, he said: Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the two rak’ahs at noon and afternoon. The first two are called Umm al-Qur’an and two surahs, and the last two are called Umm al-Qur’an. Sometimes he used to make us hear the verse, and he used to prolong the first rak’ah of the prayer. \"noon\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1037","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, and on the authority of Abu Salamah. He is Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qatada, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He would recite at noon and afternoon in the first two rak'ahs the Fatihah of the Book and two surahs, and he would sometimes make us hear the verse, and he would prolong the rak'ah. The first is at noon and he shortens the second, and likewise in the morning.”"
"1038","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “He used to recite at noon and afternoon: ‘And the sky with the constellations’, ‘And the sky’, ‘Al-Tariq’ and the like.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1039","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abd al-Rahman, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, it is recited at noon and at night when it is cloudy, and in the afternoon like that, and in the morning longer than that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1040","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Attaf told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, he said: We entered upon Anas bin Malik, and he said: Did you pray? We said: Yes. He said: O maid, come and perform ablution for me. I have not prayed behind an imam. The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more similar to the prayer of your imam. “This,” Zaid said: Omar ibn Abdul Aziz used to perform bowing and prostration completely, and he made standing and sitting easy."
"1041","Harun bin Abdullah Al-Hammal told me, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “I have never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was more similar to the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than so-and-so,” he said. Suleiman: “He used to lengthen the first two rak’ahs of the noon prayer, shorten the last two rak’ahs, shorten the afternoon prayer, and recite short and detailed rak’ahs in Maghrib. He recites in the evening in the middle of the mufassal, and in the morning he recites the length of the mufassal.”"
"1042","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “I have never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was more similar to the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than so-and-so. So we prayed behind that man, and he used to lengthen the first two verses of the noon prayer, and shorten the last two verses, and lengthen the afternoon verses, and recite during the sunset prayers. With a short, detailed verse, and it is recited in the evening with the sun and the morning prayer and the like, and it is recited in the morning with two long surahs.”"
"1043","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Jabir, he said: A man from the Ansar passed by. They poured water on Muadh, while he was praying the Maghrib prayer, so he opened Surah Al-Baqarah, and the man prayed, then he went away, and that was conveyed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “A trial, O Mu’adh? A trial, O Mu’adh? Have you not recited, ‘Glory be to the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘By the sun and its brightness’ and the like?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1044","Amr bin Mansour, who is Abu Sa`id al-Nasa’i, told us, trustworthy and proven. He said: Musa bin Dawud told us. He said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salama told us. Al-Majishun, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Umm Al-Fadl, daughter of Al-Harith, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer in his house.” Maghrib, so he recited the mursalat and then prayed another prayer until he, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested.”"
"1045","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his mother, that she heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The mursalat will be recited in Morocco.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1046","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace: “It is recited in the Maghrib prayer at Al-Tur.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1047","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us. He said: Our father, he said: Haywa, and another mentioned, they said: I am Ja`far bin Rabi’ah, that Abd Al-Rahman bin Hurmuz narrated to him that Muawiyah bin Abdullah bin Jafar narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Utba bin Masoud narrated to him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He recited during the Maghrib prayer the smoke of smoke.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1048","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, that he heard Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, He narrates on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit that he said to Marwan Aba Abd al-Malik: “Do you recite in Morocco the Qur’an, ‘He is God, the One, and indeed We have given you Al-Kawthar? He said: Yes. He said: So it is sworn. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting in it the longest of the two long vowels. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1049","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Urwa bin told me Al-Zubair, that Marwan bin Al-Hakam told him that Zayd bin Thabit said: “Why should I see you reciting in Morocco with the short part of the surah? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it at two lengths. I said: O Abu Abdullah, how long is it? He said: Al-A`raf. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1050","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: We are Baqiyah, and Abu Haywa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hamza, he said: We are Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In the Maghrib prayer, he recited Surah Al-A’raf, and divided it into two rak’ahs.”"
"1051","Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj told us, he said: Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told me, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim is Ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “I looked at the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, twenty times, and he recited the two rak’ahs.” After sunset and in the two rak'ahs before dawn, say, 'O disbelievers, and say, 'He is God, One.'\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1052","Suleiman bin Dawud, who is the son of my brother Rishdin bin Saad, told us on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: I am Amr, on the authority of Sa’id, that the father of the men Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told him, on the authority of his mother Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man on a convoy, He used to recite to his companions during their prayers, and he would end with “Say, ‘He is God, One.’” When they returned, they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he said: “Ask him for what he did that?” So they asked him, and he said: “Because it is an attribute of the Most Gracious, and I like to be recited by it.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. May God bless him and grant him peace: “Tell him that God loves him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1053","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid bin Hunayn, the client of the family of Zayd bin Al-Khattab, He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: I came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting: Say, He is God, One. {1} God Al-Samad {2} He neither begot nor was born {3} And there was no one equal to Him {4} Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is obligatory.” So I asked: What, oh? Messenger of God? He said: “Paradise.”"
"1054","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’ah, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that a man heard a man reciting: Say, He is God, One, repeating it. When morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So that was mentioned to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1055","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say it is “Allah is One, one-third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1056","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Muadh got up and prayed the evening prayer. The Hereafter, and it became long. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A trial, O Muadh? A trial, O Muadh? Where have you been when you glorified the name of your Lord, the Most High, and at dawn? And when the sky opened, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1057","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “Muadh bin Jabal, for his companions, prayed the evening prayer. So it took a long time for them, so a man from us left, and Muadh was told about him, and he said: “He is a hypocrite.” When the news reached that man, he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” So he told him what Mu’adh said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Do you want to be a seductress, O Mu’adh?” When you lead the people, recite “By the sun, and glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and by the night when it covers it, and recite in the name of your Lord.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1058","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq informed us. He said: I am my father. He said: I am Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He used to recite in the last evening prayer the verses of the sun and its dawn and similar surahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1059","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, he said: “I prayed With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the dark night, he recited therein “the figs and the olives.”"
"1060","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, so in the evening prayer in the first rak’ah he recited “figs and olives.”"
"1061","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Aoun told me, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samra. He says: Omar said to Saad: “People have doubts about everything, even about prayer.” So he said: “I extend the first two verses and delete the last two verses, and they are not the same.” I followed him from the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: That is what he thought of you."
"1062","Hammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Dawud, who is Al-Tai, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Samurah said: “Some people from the people of Kufa met Sa’d with Omar, and they said: By God, he does not pray well. So he said: As for me, I am praying a prayer.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I do not denote any of them. I am stagnant in the first two, and omitted in the last two. He said: That is the suspicion of you."
"1063","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I know the isotopes that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite twenty surahs in ten rak’ahs, then he took Alqamah by the hand and entered and then came out to us. Alqamah, so we asked him and he told us about them.”"
"1064","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Wael, saying: he said A man was with Abdullah. I recited Al-Mufassal in a rak’ah. He said: “This is like this poetry! I knew the counterparts that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had.” He said hello, linking them together and mentioning twenty surahs from al-Mufassal, two surahs in each rak’ah."
"1065","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: We are Abdullah bin Raja’, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Abdullah, and a man came to him and said: “Tonight I recited al-Mufassal in one rak’ah,” and he said: “This is like this poetry!” But The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Al-Nazir twenty surahs from Al-Mufassal, and Al-Ham.”"
"1066","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abbad told me, a hadith that he attributed to Ibn Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, said: I attended the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest, and he prayed in front of the Kaaba, so he took off his He put on his shoes and placed them on his left, so he opened Surah Al-Mu'minin, and when the mention of Moses or Jesus came, a cough took hold of him, so he bowed down. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1067","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Yahya, Abd al-Rahman, and Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustadawrid Ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah Ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah: “He prayed next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. So he recited, and whenever he came across a sign of punishment, he would stop and seek refuge, and whenever he came across a sign of mercy, he would stop and pray, and he would say while bowing: “Glory be to my Lord.” “The Great,” and in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1068","Muhammad ibn Adam informed me, on the authority of Hafs ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Talha ibn Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “He recited Al-Baqarah, the family of Imran, and the women in one rak’ah. He did not pass by a sign of mercy without asking, nor by a sign of punishment without seeking protection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1069","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Qudamah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Jasra bint Dajjah told me, she said: I heard Abu Dharr said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose until morning with a sign, and the verse is: If you punish them, they are your servants, and if you forgive To them, for You are the Mighty, the Wise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1070","Ahmad bin Mani’ and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Hushaym told us, he said: I am Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: And do not recite your prayer loudly, nor do it quietly, he said: “It was revealed while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hidden in Mecca. When he led his companions in prayer, he raised his voice.” Ibn Mani’ said: “He recited the Qur’an aloud, but when the polytheists heard it, they reviled the Qur’an and whoever sent it down.” And whoever brings it, “God said to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: And do not recite your prayer out loud, that is, with your recitation, lest the polytheists hear and curse.” the Qur’an, and do not frighten your companions thereby, lest they listen, and seek a way in between. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1071","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his voice reciting the Qur’an, and when the polytheists heard his voice they would curse the Qur’an and whoever brought it, and so it was. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lowered his voice when he recited the Qur’an. His companions did not hear him, so God revealed “And do not be loud in your prayer and do not be afraid.” Therein and seek a way between these (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1072","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Waki', he said: We are Mas'ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja'dah, on the authority of Umm Hani, She said: “I was listening to the recitation of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was on my throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1073","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I asked Anas, how was the recitation of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “He used to extend his voice out loud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1074","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”"
"1075","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Talha told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” Ibn Awsaja said: I had forgotten this. Beautify the Qur’an,” until Al-Dahhak Ibn Muzahim reminded me of it."
"1076","Muhammad bin Zanbour told us, he said: Ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God has not authorized anything unless He has authorized a prophet with a beautiful voice with the Qur’an.” \"He speaks it out loud\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1077","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “God has not authorized anything that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has not authorized, singing the Qur’an.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: “His permission” did not I understood it as I wanted (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1078","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Ibn Shihab told him that Abu Salamah, He told him that Abu Hurairah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard Abu Musa reciting, and he said: He was given some of the Psalms of the Almighty. David"
"1079","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar told us that Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, read Abu Musa’s recitation, and he said: “This was given to me from the Psalms of the family of David.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1080","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, he said: we were told by Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: he heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read Abu Musa’s recitation, and he said: “This man was given a psalm from the psalms of the family of David.”"
"1081","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ali bin Mamluk He asked Umm Salamah about the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his prayers. She said: What do you have to do with his prayers? Then his reading was described to him, so it was “a reading interpreted letter by letter.”"
"1082","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah, When Marwan made him his successor in charge of Medina, when he stood to perform the obligatory prayer he would say “Allahu Akbar,” and then he would say “Allahu Akbar” when he bowed, then when he raised his head from rak’ah, he said: “God hears whoever praises Him. Our Lord, and to You is praise.” Then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he falls prostrating, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he gets up from the two, after The tashahhud, then he does the same thing until he finishes his prayer. When he finishes his prayer and gives the salutation, he goes to the people of the mosque, and he says: By the one My soul is in His hand. Indeed, “I resemble your prayers to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1083","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim Al-Laythi, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his hands when he said “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, until they reached branches. \"His ears\""
"1084","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “When he begins the prayer, he raises his hands until they are in line with his shoulders, and when he bows, and when he raises his head after bowing.”"
"1085","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah On the authority of Abdullah, he said: Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “So he stood up and raised his hands the first time, then he did not raise them.”"
"1086","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A prayer is not sufficient in which a man does not straighten his cross while bowing and prostrating.”"
"1087","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am a servant of God, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Orouba, and Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be moderate in bowing and prostrating, and do not let any of you spread out his arms like a dog.”"
"1088","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asam, he said: Anas bin Malik was asked about the takbeer in Prayer, and he said: “He says takbir when he bows, when he prostrates, when he raises his head from prostration, and when he stands from the two rak’ahs.” Hutaym said: From whom? Do you save this? He said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and Omar. Then he remained silent, and he said to him: Hateem: And Othman? He said: And Othman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1089","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Ghailan bin Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, he said: Ali bin Abi Talib prayed, and he used to say “Allahu Akbar” with every lowering and raising of his voice, completing the “Allahu Akbar.” Imran said: This reminded me of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace"
"1090","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, and the pronunciation is his, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul told me Al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: Muhammad bin Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Humaid Al-Sa’idi, he said: I heard him speaking, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He said: “When he stands up from the two prostrations, he says ‘Allahu Akbar’ and raises his hands until he aligns them with his shoulders, as he did when he opened the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1091","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He would raise his hands when he entered into prayer, and when he wanted to bow, and when he raised his head after bowing, And when he stands from the two rak’ahs, he raises his hands in the same way as the shoes of his shoulders.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1092","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: We were Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la, he said: Ubaid Allah, who is Ibn Umar, told us, on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out to reconcile the Banu Amr bin Awf, and the time for prayer came. Then the muezzin came to Abu Bakr and ordered him to gather the people and lead them in prayer. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and broke through the rows. Until he stood in the front row, and the people greeted Abu Bakr to call him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr did not turn around. Prayer, and when they had increased, he knew that something had disturbed them in their prayer, so he turned around, and behold, it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he nodded. To him is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that is, as you are. Abu Bakr raised his hands and thanked God and praised him for what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had said. Then the one who left behind came back, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and prayed. When he left, he said to Abu Bakr: “What prevented you, when Did I motion for you to pray?” Abu Bakr said: It was not appropriate for Ibn Abi Quhafa to lead the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then. He said to the people: “What is the matter with you that you forgive? Forgiveness is only for women.” Then he said: “If anything of your prayer bothers you, say the Sublime.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1093","Qutaibah told us, he said: Na Abtar, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim ibn Tarfa, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us while we were raising our hands in prayer, and he said: “What is the matter with them raising their hands in prayer? As if they were the tails of horses, the sun. Be still in prayer.”"
"1094","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Qibtiyyah, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, He said: We used to pray behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would salute with our hands. He said: “What is the matter with these people who salute with their hands, as if they were horses’ tails?” Sun? Isn’t it enough for one of them to put his hand on his thigh and then say: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1095","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Nabul, the owner of the cloak, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Suhayb, the companion of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I passed by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he responded to me with a gesture, but there was no I know, except that he said with his finger.”"
"1096","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, Ibn Umar said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Quba Mosque to pray in, then men entered it to greet him, so I asked Suhaib who was with him, “How did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, do?” When he greeted him, he said: He was gesturing with his hand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1097","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Wahb told us, meaning Ibn Jarir, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Ali, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser: “He greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and he responded to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1098","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me Because of his need, then I caught him while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he pointed to me. When he finished, he called me and said: “You greeted me just now, and I I pray, but he is then facing toward the east.”"
"1099","Muhammad bin Hashim Al-Baalbaki told us, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, he said: Abu told me Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me, so I came to him while he was walking in the east and the west, so I greeted him, and he indicated with his hand, then I greeted him, and he gestured with his hand, so I left, and the people called me: O Jabir, so I went to him and said: O Messenger of God, I greeted you, but you did not He responded to me and said: “I was praying.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: They claimed that this hadith in Egypt was not the hadith of Amr ibn al-Harith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1100","Qutayba bin Saeed and Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you stands for prayer, he does not wipe away the pebbles, for mercy will confront him.”"
"1101","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, on the authority of Abdullah, who is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Mu’aqib told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you are a doer, then it is a sin.”"
"1102","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi and Shu`aib ibn Yusuf al-Nasa’i informed us, on the authority of Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa`id al-Qattan, on the authority of Ibn Abu Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the matter with people who raise Their eyes to the sky during their prayer? Then his speech intensified about that, until he said: “Shall they refrain from that, or their eyes will be snatched away?”"
"1103","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah A man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If “One of you is praying and does not raise his gaze to the sky, lest his gaze shine.”"
"1104","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am a servant of God, he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, He told us in the gathering of Ibn al-Musayyab, and Ibn al-Musayyab was sitting, that he heard Abu Dharr say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” God continues to face the servant during his prayer as long as he does not turn away, then if he turns his face away, he turns away from Him.”"
"1105","Amr bin Ali told us, Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Zaida, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’atha, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning away during prayer, and he said: “It is an embezzlement by Satan that steals from prayer.” Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly, Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Ash’ath Ibn Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Abu Atiya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1106","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, Al-Mu’affa told me, who is Ibn Sulaiman, Al-Qasim, who is Ibn Ma’n, told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abi Atiyah said: Aisha said: “Growing around during prayer is an embezzlement that Satan steals from the prayer.”"
"1107","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. So we prayed behind him, while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr was saying “Allahu Akbar” so people could hear him saying “Allahu Akbar.” He turned to us and saw us standing, so he pointed to us. We sat and prayed his prayer, sitting, and when he greeted him, he said: “Indeed, you were just about to do the actions of the Persians and the Romans, who rise up against their kings, and they Sitting, do not do so. Follow your imams. If he prays standing, then pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting.”"
"1108","Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Thawr bin Zaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to turn right and left in his prayer, and did not twist his neck behind him. \"His back\""
"1109","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Yazid, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Dammam, on the authority of Abi Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of the two lions during prayer.”"
"1110","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Sulayman bin Dawud Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Dammam, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He ordered the killing of the two lions during prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1111","Qutaibah told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray while holding the imamate, so when he prostrated, he placed it down, and when he stood, he raised it.”"
"1112","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr Ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, leading the people in prayer while he was carrying Umamah, the daughter of Abu Al-Aas, on his shoulder. So when he bows, he places it, and when he finishes his prostration, he repeats it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1113","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Hatim bin Wardan, he said: Burd bin Sinan Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I opened the door, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying voluntarily, and the door was facing the Qiblah, so he walked to his right.” Or to his left, then he opened the door, then returned to his place of prayer.”"
"1114","Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, and the wording is his. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.” Ibn Al-Muthanna added: “In prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1115","Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah informed me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, they heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1116","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman Al-A’mash. On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.”"
"1117","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Muhammad told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1118","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, meaning Al-Ukli, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr, he said: We Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, said: “I had an hour with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I went to him. When I came to him, I asked for permission. If I find him praying, say the Sublime, I will enter, and if I find him empty, give me permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1119","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, he said: “I came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, and there was a buzzing inside his stomach like the buzzing of a boiler, meaning: he was crying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1120","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi told me, he said: We are Ibn Ayyash, meaning Abu Bakr, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Ibn Naji, who said: Ali said: “I had two entrances to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: an entrance at night, and an entrance during the day. I came in at night, and he bowed his throat to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1121","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Sharhabeel told me, meaning Ibn Mudarrak, he said: Abdullah told me. Ibn Naji, on the authority of his father, said: Ali said: “I had a status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that no other creature had, so I was I come to him every dawn and say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet of God. If he clears his throat, I go back to my family, otherwise I go in on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1122","Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Rabi’ah ibn Yazid narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Idris. Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, and we heard him say: “I seek refuge in God from you.” Then he said He said: “I curse you with the curse of God” three times, and he extended his hand as if he was eating something. When he finished praying, we said: O Messenger of God, we heard you say Is there anything in prayer that we have not heard you say before, and we saw you spread your hand? ! He said: “The enemy of God, Satan, came with a shooting star to strike my face, so I said: I seek refuge in God from you three times, then I said: I curse you.” By the curse of God, he did not delay it three times. Then I wanted to take him. By God, had it not been for the call of our brother Suleiman, he would have been bound, playing. Therein are the children of the people of Medina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1123","Kathir bin Ubaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to prayer, and we stood with him, and a Bedouin said while he was in prayer: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on us. One day, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, he said to the Bedouins: “You have become greatly petrified,” seeking God’s mercy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1124","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Save him from Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa`id told me, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that a Bedouin entered the mosque, prayed two rak’ahs, then said: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on anyone with us, so the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “You have become largely petrified.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1125","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maimunah said: Ata bin Yassar told me, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, this is a hadith A covenant of ignorance, then God brought Islam, and some of us were praising Him. He said: “That is something they find in their chests, so do not stop them.” And some of us go to soothsayers. He said: “But do not go to them.” He said: O Messenger of God, and some of us call calligraphers. He said: “There was a prophet from among the prophets.” He writes, so whoever agrees with his handwriting, that is it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1126","He said: While I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in prayer, a man from among the people sneezed, so I said: May God have mercy on you, and the people stared at me. With their eyes, so I said: I am bereft of the illiterate, why are you looking at me? ! He said: The people hit their hands on their thighs, and when I saw them silence me, I remained silent, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left He called me by my father and my mother. He did not hit me, nor curse me, nor curse me. I have never seen a teacher before him or after him with better teaching than him. He said: “Indeed In this prayer of ours, nothing of what people say is appropriate. Rather, it is glorification and glorification, and recitation of the Qur’an.”"
"1127","He said: Then I looked at a spoil of mine that was being tended by a maid of mine in front of Uhud and next to me, and when I looked up, I found that the wolf had taken some of it from a sheep. And I am a man from the children of Adam, and I am sorry as they are sorry, so I minted it in a surety, then I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. This was very difficult for me, so I said: O Messenger of God, should I not free her? He said: “Call her.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Where is God?” She said: In heaven. He said: “Who am I?” She said: You are the Messenger. God said: “She is a believer, so free her.”"
"1128","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, he said: Al-Harith bin Shubail told me On the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: “A man used to speak to his companion during prayer about a need, at the time of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And peace be upon him, until this verse was revealed: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer and stand obedient to God.” So he commanded us to remain silent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1129","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili informed me, saying: Ibn Abi Ghaniyah, and Al-Qasim means Ibn Yazid Al-Jarmi, told us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adi, on the authority of Kulthum, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, and this is the hadith of Al-Qasim, he said: I used to go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello while he was praying, so I said hello to him, and he responded to me. So I went to him and said hello to him, while he was praying, but he did not respond to me. When he said hello, he pointed to The people, and he said: “God, meaning, has enjoined prayer, that you should not speak except in the remembrance of God, and it is not befitting for you to stand up to God in obedience.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1130","Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: We used to greet The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned our greetings, until we came from the land of Abyssinia, so I greeted him, but he did not respond to me, so he took me almost And after that, I sat until when he had finished the prayer, he said: “Indeed, God creates His command whatever He wills, and indeed He has created His command that no one should speak about it.” \"Prayer\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1131","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buhayna, he said: “The Messenger of God prayed for us May God bless him and grant him peace, he prayed two rak'ahs, then he stood up and did not sit down, so the people stood up with him. When he finished his prayer, and we saw his greeting, he said takbeer and prostrated. He prostrated two times while he was sitting before the salutation, then he saluted.”"
"1132","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buhayna, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He stood up during prayer and was required to sit, so he prostrated two prostrations while he was sitting before the salutation.”"
"1133","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: I am Yazid, and he is Ibn Zuray’. He said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led one of the evening prayers for us. He said: Abu Hurairah said: But I forgot. He said: “So he led for us two rak’ahs. Then he said his salutations, and went to an exposed piece of wood in the mosque, and said with his hand on it as if he was angry, and the two dragons came out of the doors. The mosque. They said: The prayer was shortened. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Omar, so they were afraid to speak to him. Among the people was a man with a long hand. He said: He was called Dhul-Yadin, and he said: O Messenger of God, did you forget or was the prayer shortened? He said: “I have not forgotten, and the prayer has not been shortened.” He said: And he said: “As the one with two hands says?” They said: Yes, so he came. The one who had left prayed, then said the salaam. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated like his prostration, or longer. Then he raised his head and said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he prostrated like his prostration, or longer. Then he raised his head and said “Allahu Akbar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1134","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ayoub told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left after two days, and Dhul-Yadin said to him: Did you shorten the prayer or did you forget, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did the one with two hands speak the truth?” The people said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed. Two times, then he said the salaam, then he said “Allahu Akbar”, so he prostrated like his prostration, or longer, then he raised his head, then he said “Allahu Akbar”, so he prostrated like his prostration, or It was longer and then raised.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1135","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, the client of Ibn Abi Ahmad, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the afternoon prayer for us, so he gave the salutation in two rak’ahs, then Dhu al-Yadin stood up and said: Did you shorten the prayer, O Messenger of God, or did you forget? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of that did not happen.” He said: Some of that happened, O. Messenger of God, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached the people and said: “Does the one with two hands tell the truth?” They said: Yes. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, completed what remained of the prayer, then he prostrated two prostrations while he was sitting after the salutation."
"1136","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Bahz, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that he heard Abu Salamah speaking, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed the noon prayer two rak’ahs, then he gave the salutation. They said: Has the prayer been shortened? So he got up and prayed.” He performed two rak'ahs, then he said the salaam, then he prostrated two prostrations.\""
"1137","Issa bin Hammad - Zaghba - informed us, saying: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed one day, and said the salaam in two rak’ahs, then he left, and Dhu al-Shamalayn overtook him, and said: O Messenger of God, was the prayer shortened or did you forget? He said: “The prayer did not diminish, and I did not forget.” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one with two hands is most truthful.” “They said: Yes,” and he led the people in prayer two rak’ahs."
"1138","Harun bin Musa told me, he said: Abu Damra told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forgot, so he gave the salutation in two prostrations, and Dhu al-Shamalayn said to him: Did you shorten the prayer or did you forget, oh? Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Does the one with two hands tell the truth?” They said: Yes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and completed the prayer."
"1139","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, and my father Bakr bin Sulaiman bin Abi Hathamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon or afternoon prayer, so he gave the salutation in two rak’ahs. He left, and Dhu al-Shamalayn ibn Amr said to him: Was the prayer shortened or did you forget? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What do those with two hands say?” So they said: “He spoke the truth, O Prophet of God, so complete with them the two rak’ahs which he missed.” Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub told us, he said: Abi told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah told him that he had heard that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs, and he said: He has Dhu al-Shamalayn, something like that. Ibn Shihab: This news was told to me by Sa’id ibn al-Musayyib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman told me, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith, and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1140","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Uqail, who said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, on the authority of Sa’id. And Abu Salamah, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, and Ibn Abi Hathamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate May peace be upon him on that day, before or after the greeting of peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1141","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Wahb, he said: I am Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of A’rak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He prostrated on the Day of The hands prostrated after the salutation.” Amr ibn Sawad told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: I am Amr ibn al-Harith, he said: Qatada told me, On the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1142","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar, a Homsi, told me. He said: Na Baqiya. He said: Shu’bah told me. He said: Tell me. Ibn Aoun, and Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prostrated in his state of mind after the salutation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1143","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, On the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed with them, but he broke it and prostrated.” Then he greeted (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1144","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Zuray’, he said: Khalid Al-Hadha’ told us, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: He greeted the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in three rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer. He entered, and a man called Al-Kharbaq stood up to him and said: Prayer. O Messenger of God, so he came out angrily, dragging his cloak, and said: “Is he telling the truth?” They said: Yes, so he stood up and prayed that rak’ah, then said the salaam, then prostrated. You prostrated to her, then he said salaam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1145","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him remove the doubt, and build on certainty. “If he is completely awake, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1146","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ informed us, he said: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is Ibn Abi Salamah, informed us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, On the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If one of you does not know how many times he has prayed three times or Should he pray four rak'ahs, then perform two prostrations after that, while sitting? If he prayed five, then his prayers will be interceded for him. Four, they were an incentive for Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1147","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told me, he said: Mufaddal, and he is Ibn Muhalhalil, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, attributes it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him investigate if he thinks that it is correct.” The correct thing is, so he should complete it and then, that is, prostrate two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1148","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami told us, he said: We are Waki’, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him be careful and prostrate.” Two prostrations after he finishes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1149","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, whether it was more or less, and it was said: O Messenger of God, did anything happen in the prayer? He said: “If something had happened, I would have informed you about it, but I am only human and forget just as you forget. So whoever of you has any doubts about his prayer, let him consider it better.” This leads to what is right, so let him complete it, then let him greet, and prostrate two prostrations.”"
"1150","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman Al-Mujalidi told me, he said: I am Al-Fudayl, and he is Ibn Iyaad, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer, whether he added more or less of it, and when he said the salutation, we said: O Prophet of God Did anything happen during prayer? He said: “And what was that?” He said: So We mentioned to him what he had done, so he bent his leg and faced the Qiblah, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he turned to the Qiblah. On us to his face, and he said: “If something had happened in prayer, I would have informed you of it.” Then he said: “I am only human like you. I forget just as you forget. “So whoever of you forgets something in his prayer, let him investigate what he thinks is correct, then he should say the salutation and then perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1151","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Mansour wrote to me, and I read it to him, And I heard him telling a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the noon prayer, then He turned to them with his face, and they said: Something happened during prayer. He said: “And what was that?” So they told him what he had done, so he bent his foot and faced. facing the qiblah, so he prostrated two prostrations, then he saluted, then he turned to them with his face and said: “I am only human like you. I forget as you forget.” So if I forget, remind me.” He said: And he said: “If something happened during prayer, I would inform you.” He said: And he said: “If one of you misleads in prayer, So let him look for the closest thing to what is correct, then let him complete it, then let him prostrate two prostrations.”"
"1152","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Wael, saying: Abdullah said: “Who If he is delusional in his prayer, let him determine what is correct, then prostrate two prostrations after he has finished while sitting.”"
"1153","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am a servant of God, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Whoever doubts or If he is deluded, let him be careful, then let him prostrate two prostrations.”"
"1154","Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Musafa’ said, on the authority of Utbah bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is in doubt about his prayer, let him prostrate two times.” after he greets\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1155","Muhammad bin Hashim told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Musafa’, on the authority of Utba bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has doubts about his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations after the salutation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
